# Vercel Web Analytics Integration

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Vite + React project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
- Retrieved the most up-to-date installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Identified that this is a Vite + React project requiring the React-specific integration

### 2. Package Installation
- The `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) was already listed in package.json
- Ran `npm install` to ensure the package and all dependencies were properly installed
- Generated `package-lock.json` to lock dependency versions

### 3. Analytics Integration
**Modified: `src/App.tsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the main app div
- This follows the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite projects

### 4. Verification
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed with no errors
- ✅ Package properly installed and types available
- ✅ Dependencies locked in package-lock.json
- ✅ Code follows existing project structure and conventions

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added to `App.tsx` following the official Vercel documentation pattern for React/Vite applications. The component will automatically:
- Track page views when deployed to Vercel
- Send analytics data to the Vercel Analytics dashboard
- Work in both development and production environments

## Next Steps (for deployment)
1. Deploy the app to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics tab)
3. Verify analytics are working by checking the Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`
4. Monitor analytics data in the Vercel dashboard

## Files Modified
- `src/App.tsx` - Added Analytics component
- `package.json` - Alphabetically sorted by npm (no functional changes)
- `package-lock.json` - Created to lock dependency versions
